after the rocky launch of no man's sky  hello games all but fell off the radar  now they're back with the long-awaited  foundation update to be here to tuck  into the foundation update introduces  base building to the game and serves as  a quilt foundation for things to come as  the name implies in a post on their  website hello games explained that this  marks the first of many free patches for  no man's sky the update also adds three  new game modes featuring different rule  sets normal mode which is what you're  used to from the first iteration  creative mode which lets you explore the  universe without limits and build a huge  base and survival mode which is a more  challenging endurance experience face  building will enable you to create an  outpost using modular structures and  decorations made using resources you  find while exploring the game world  you'll also be able to recruit alien  life-forms to help research new tech use  terminus teleporters in space stations  to get to and from your base with ease  expand your base with storage containers  to stockpile resources and dismantle  your previous homestead to refund all  your resources the update will allow you  to farm purchase and customize  freighters to transfer resources  discover new resource types and craft  new items there are also visual upgrades  like motion blur temporal anti-aliasing  and new UI indicators including better  representations of shield and life  support changes there's also now a photo  mode on ps4 no man's sky creator Sean  Murray has tweeted if you could have  lived our lives over the last month's  you'd know how meaningful this is check  out our story on site for the full patch  notes and let me know what you think of  the changes in that comment section for  everything else that matters in gaming  stay tuned to gamespot
 

